    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Owner Dmitry Nagiyev is giving a grand tour of his restaurant to his friend Igor. He proudly shows off the staff and the decor. Let's listen closely to their exchange in Russian first, and then walk through each line together.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "nagiyev",
      "t": "Вот, Игорь.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "nagiyev",
      "t": "Это оазис французской кухни.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "nagiyev",
      "t": "Анклав качества.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "nagiyev",
      "t": "Сколько сил вложено сюда.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "nagiyev",
      "t": "Официант, как родной ребенок.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "nagiyev",
      "t": "О, привет, Виляш.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "nastya",
      "t": "Я Настя, вообще-то.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "nagiyev",
      "t": "Новенькая, наверное.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "nagiyev",
      "t": "Ну, пойдем дальше.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "nagiyev",
      "t": "Сделай нам два кофе.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "nagiyev",
      "t": "Это Виктория Сергеевна.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "nagiyev",
      "t": "Арт-директор нашего ресторана.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Добрый день.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Let's walk through it together.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "nagiyev",
      "t": "Вот, Игорь.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Here you go, Igor.' — Built around the key proper name meaning 'Igor'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "nagiyev",
      "t": "Это оазис французской кухни.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'This is an oasis of French cuisine.' Notice the word order: 'this' comes first, and 'kitchen' finishes the sentence.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "nagiyev",
      "t": "Анклав качества.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'A bastion of quality.' Here 'enclave' sets up the idea, while 'quality' comes at the end for emphasis.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "nagiyev",
      "t": "Сколько сил вложено сюда.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'So much effort went into this place.' You'll hear 'how much' all the time in the show, here connected with 'here'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "nagiyev",
      "t": "Официант, как родной ребенок.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'A waiter is like my own child.' The question word for 'how' comes right at the start, followed directly by 'child'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "nagiyev",
      "t": "О, привет, Виляш.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Oh, hi, Vilyash.' Nagiyev starts with 'hi' and pairs it with 'Vilyash' to make the point clear.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "nastya",
      "t": "Я Настя, вообще-то.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I am Nastya, actually.' Nastya puts 'I' up front so the listener immediately catches the tone, followed by 'Nastya'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "nagiyev",
      "t": "Новенькая, наверное.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'She must be new.' In Russian, 'new girl' leads into 'probably' in a very natural everyday phrasing.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "nagiyev",
      "t": "Ну, пойдем дальше.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Well, let's keep going.' The first content word means 'let's go', and 'next' rounds out the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "nagiyev",
      "t": "Сделай нам два кофе.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Make us two coffees.' A compact expression built around 'make' and 'of coffee'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "nagiyev",
      "t": "Это Виктория Сергеевна.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'This is Viktoria Sergeyevna.' Listen for the word meaning 'this' right alongside 'Viktoriya' in this line.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "nagiyev",
      "t": "Арт-директор нашего ресторана.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'The art director of our restaurant.' Russian leaves out 'am', 'is', or 'are' in the present tense, linking 'art director' straight to 'restaurant'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Добрый день.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Good afternoon.' Notice the word order: 'good' comes first, and 'day' finishes the sentence.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
